{
  "name": "Generate unit tests for GitHub pull requests with Claude and run them in CI",
  "flow": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "module": "gateway:CustomWebHook",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {
        "maxResults": 1
      },
      "mapper": {},
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Webhook: Receive the PR and diff"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "config_your_name",
            "value": "Your name — signs every outgoing message"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_email",
            "value": "you@example.com"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_company",
            "value": "Your company or brokerage"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_timezone",
            "value": "Europe/London"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_start",
            "value": "21"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_end",
            "value": "8"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approval_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approver",
            "value": "#approvals — a Slack channel, or an email address"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_test_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_schedule",
            "value": "instant (webhook)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 300,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Config (edit me)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "result",
            "value": ""
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 600,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Find untested changed functions (port the rule here)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "module": "github:createAComment",
      "version": 4,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "owner": "{{1.owner}}",
        "repository": "{{1.repo}}",
        "issue_number": "{{1.number}}",
        "body": "{{1.summary}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 900,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "GitHub: Assemble context"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "module": "anthropic-claude:createAMessage",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "system": "You are the \"Generate tests\" step of the Unit Test Generation Workflow workflow run by Agentmelt.\nTask: Tests per function in the repo's framework and style, covering the happy path, edge cases visible in the code, and error paths; structured output with one test file per source file.\n\nRules:\n- Generated tests are proposed in a separate PR; nothing merges without an engineer's review.\n- Only tests that pass, are not flaky, and add coverage are proposed — the run is the filter.\n- The agent cannot modify source code, only add test files.\n- Repositories can be excluded, and a self-hosted model is available for sensitive code.\n- Answer only from the data provided in the input. If something is missing, say so in the output instead of guessing.\n- If this step produces a message or a document, put the full text in `draft` (and a `subject` if it is an email); put a one-line summary in `summary`.\n- Set `needs_human` true whenever you are unsure, the input is unusual, or a rule above applies; a person will look at it.\n- Return valid JSON matching the output schema; no prose outside the JSON.\n\nReply with a single JSON object and nothing else: the fields the task needs, plus \"needs_human\" (true when unsure), \"confidence\" (0–1) and \"summary\" (one line).",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Generate tests.\n\nItem (map the fields your source provides here):\n{{4.text}}{{4.body}}{{4.message}}{{4.subject}}{{4.email}}{{4.name}}{{4.data}}"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "max_tokens": "2000",
        "temperature": "0.2",
        "metadata": {}
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1200,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Claude: Generate tests"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "module": "json:ParseJSON",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "json": "{{5.textResponse}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1500,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Parse Claude's JSON: Generate tests"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": null,
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1800,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Gate: Generate tests"
        }
      },
      "routes": [
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 11,
              "module": "builtin:ThrowWarning",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "message": "Parked for a person — Generate tests: {{6.summary}}"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2100,
                  "y": 0,
                  "name": "Needs a person: Generate tests"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Needs a person?",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{6.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:equal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 7,
              "module": "github:createAComment",
              "version": 4,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "owner": "{{6.owner}}",
                "repository": "{{6.repo}}",
                "issue_number": "{{6.number}}",
                "body": "{{6.summary}}"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2100,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "GitHub: Run in CI"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Continue",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{6.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:notequal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 8,
              "module": "util:SetVariables",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": {
                "scope": "roundtrip",
                "variables": [
                  {
                    "name": "confidence",
                    "value": "{{6.confidence}}"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2400,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Keep what passes and adds coverage (add a filter on the next module)"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 9,
              "module": "github:createAComment",
              "version": 4,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "owner": "{{7.owner}}",
                "repository": "{{7.repo}}",
                "issue_number": "{{7.number}}",
                "body": "{{6.summary}}"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2700,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "GitHub: Open the companion PR"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 10,
              "module": "util:SetVariables",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": {
                "scope": "roundtrip",
                "variables": [
                  {
                    "name": "run_at",
                    "value": "{{now}}"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 3000,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Learn from reviews (runs on the scenario schedule)"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "instant": true,
    "version": 1,
    "scenario": {
      "roundtrips": 1,
      "maxErrors": 3,
      "autoCommit": true,
      "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
      "sequential": false,
      "slots": null,
      "confidential": false,
      "dataloss": false,
      "dlq": false,
      "freshVariables": false
    },
    "designer": {
      "orphans": []
    },
    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Generate unit tests for GitHub pull requests with Claude and run them in CI\n\nEngineering teams with thin test coverage who want tests proposed automatically on every change.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: PR events on the main repositories; a label can request generation on demand.\n1. Receive the PR and diff\n2. Find untested changed functions\n3. Assemble context\n4. Generate tests\n5. Run in CI\n6. Keep what passes and adds coverage\n7. Open the companion PR\n8. Learn from reviews\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus GitHub Actions / GitLab CI, Jest / pytest / Go test / JUnit.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the test framework and directories in the Config node; swap the GitHub nodes for GitLab if that is where the code lives.\nGuardrail to keep: Generated tests are proposed in a separate PR; nothing merges without an engineer's review.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/unit-test-generation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}